.TH tapectl-volume-write 1  "tapectl-volume-write " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-volume\-write \- Write staged data to volume
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl volume write\fR [\fB\-\-device\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-missing\-escrow\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fILABEL\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Write staged data to volume
.PP
Refuses any volume not left `initialized` by `volume init` — a sealed, retired, erased or quarantined volume is not a write target (ADR\-0012); no flag overrides it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-device\fR \fI<DEVICE>\fR
Tape device (by\-id path). Defaults to the only configured drive; required when more than one is configured
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes. Commands that cannot preview refuse the flag rather than ignore it (issue #241)
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
See `volume init \-\-force` — same override, same limits
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-missing\-escrow\fR
Seal slices that were staged before the escrow recipient existed (ADR\-0005). Only reachable for tapes copied forward via `read\-slices`/`compact\-read`, since `stage create` refuses to stage without escrow; use it to migrate a dying pre\-escrow cartridge, knowing the copy stays unrecoverable by the escrow key
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip ADR\-0008 Tier\-2 confirmation prompts. It never reaches a Tier\-3 refusal — those are facts, not risks to accept (issue #147)
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file.

NOTE: on its own this ALSO relocates the whole tapectl home to the config file\*(Aqs parent directory — database, keys, staging, receipts. That is how every test harness gets an isolated home, so it still works, but it is surprising enough that it now warns. Use \-\-home when you mean "operate on a different archive", and \-\-config only to point at a config file inside that home (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
tapectl home directory: database, keys, catalogs, receipts, logs.

Defaults to ~/.tapectl. The config file is taken from <home>/config.toml unless \-\-config overrides it. Also settable as TAPECTL_HOME (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fILABEL\fR>
Volume label
